.TITLE "dmesg"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Prints the message buffer of the Linux kernel. It is primarily used to __diagnose hardware__ issues, driver problems, and boot sequence messages.

.DIV "TLDR"
**dmesg**
Displays all messages currently stored in the kernel ring buffer.
> 

**dmesg -H**
Displays kernel messages in a human-friendly format with colors and a pager.
> __-H__ human-friendly flag

**dmesg -w**
Waits for new kernel messages and displays them as they appear in real-time.
> __-w__ follow flag

**dmesg -l level**
Filters the output to show only messages with a specific log level (e.g., err, warn).
> __-l__ level flag | __level__ message priority level

.DIV "SUMMARY"
If you plug in a new USB device or experience a hardware failure, __dmesg__ is the first place you should look for error messages. It provides a direct window into how the kernel is interacting with your physical hardware.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:journalctl** **linux:lsblk**

